# The deployed build has no backend to talk to: Cloudflare serves the SPA as
# static assets, so POST /api/v1/sesiones comes back 405 Method Not Allowed and
# nobody can sign in. Production builds therefore use the hardcoded demo catalog
# by default — the flag is a build-time decision, never a runtime fallback.
#
# Local development is untouched: `npm run dev` runs in development mode and does
# not read this file, so it keeps talking to the real backend through the Vite
# proxy (/api -> localhost:8080).
#
# This also covers a build run by Cloudflare itself, which invokes its own
# `npm run build` and never the `deploy:demo` script.
#
# Override it with an explicit variable, which wins over this file:
#   set VITE_DEMO_MODE=0&& npm run build
